<title>ITALY: Treasury says no date yet set for Eni sale.</title>
<headline>Treasury says no date yet set for Eni sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury said no date or official calendar has yet been set for the sale of a second tranche of shares in state energy group Eni.</p>
<p>According to a preliminary timetable obtained by Reuters, a maximum price for the share offering will be fixed on October 19 and will be published on October 20 with the share offer closing on October 25.</p>
<p>Treasury director Mario Draghi told reporters some details of the operation will be announced next week after stock market regulator Consob approves the offer prospectus.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
